      <h1>Photography + On-Site Video Shoots for Dermatology + Skin Clinics — India + GCC + International 2026 Playbook</h1>
      <p class="lede">How to plan clinic photography + video shoots for social + ads in Dermatology + Skin Clinics? This guide covers costs, tactics, tools, timelines, compliance, and real outcomes from ITD GrowthLabs&#x27; work across 20+ clinic engagements in India + GCC. We currently manage full-stack digital marketing for a premium dermatology brand with 5+ clinics across India (client name shared under NDA). Serves all major India cities (Mumbai + Delhi + Bangalore + Ahmedabad + Hyderabad + Chennai + Pune + Kolkata + Gurgaon + Noida + Jaipur + Chandigarh + Thane + Navi Mumbai + Nashik + Nagpur + Lucknow + Indore + Kochi + Coimbatore), GCC (Dubai + Abu Dhabi + Sharjah + Riyadh + Jeddah + Doha + Kuwait City + Manama + Muscat), and international markets (London + Singapore + more).</p>
      <a class="book-cta" href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-doctors.php#packages">See Packages + Book Free Growth Audit &rarr;</a>
      <div class="cities">Serving India + GCC + International: Mumbai · Delhi · Bangalore · Ahmedabad · Hyderabad · Chennai · Pune · Kolkata · Gurgaon · Noida · Jaipur · Chandigarh · Lucknow · Indore + more</div>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <div class="doc-container narrow">
        <h2>12 Answers Doctors Ask Us About Photography + On-Site Video Shoots</h2>
        <p class="lede">Analysis based on ITD GrowthLabs' work across 20+ clinic engagements in India + GCC. Client names + case study details shared on discovery call under NDA.</p>

          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Does ITD really come on-site to shoot at my dermatology clinic?</h3>
            <div>Yes — on-site photography + video shoots are a signature ITD service, particularly for Dermatology + Skin Clinics. Full team (photographer + videographer + director + lighting assistant) travels to your clinic across Mumbai metro. We bring cameras + lighting + audio + wardrobe + makeup coordination. Shoot day 4-6 hours, captures 4-8 Reels + 40-80 static photos + 2-4 long-form testimonials. Frequency: quarterly (Growth), monthly (Premium), weekly (Enterprise).</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How much does a professional dermatology clinic photo/video shoot cost?</h3>
            <div>Standalone one-day shoot: Rs 45,000 - Rs 1,80,000 depending on scope. Basic (photographer + videographer, 4-hour shoot, static + Reel content): Rs 45-75K. Standard (add director + lighting + audio + 6-hour shoot): Rs 75K-1.2L. Premium (add makeup artist + wardrobe + creative director + full-day): Rs 1.2-1.8L. When bundled into ITD's Growth+ retainer, shoots are cost-included (2-4 per year).</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What do we need to prepare at our clinic before the shoot day?</h3>
            <div>ITD's pre-shoot checklist: (1) confirm 4-6 hour block with minimal patient traffic (typically Sunday morning or Monday off-day), (2) coordinate 2-4 doctor + team on-camera participants, (3) clear + clean 3-4 procedure rooms + reception, (4) confirm consent from any patient testimonial participants, (5) approve Reel scripts 48 hours before, (6) provide 1-2 wardrobe options for on-camera doctors. ITD brings all equipment + lighting.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What content does one shoot day produce for a dermatology clinic?</h3>
            <div>Typical Growth-tier 6-hour shoot day delivers: (1) 4-8 Instagram Reels (30-60 sec each), (2) 40-80 high-res static photos (facility + team + procedure + hero shots), (3) 2-4 long-form patient testimonial videos (2-5 min for YouTube + website), (4) 1-2 doctor-on-camera educational videos (3-8 min for YouTube), (5) 10-20 GBP + WhatsApp assets. Covers 30-60 days of social + ads content.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Are before-after photos safe for dermatology clinics?</h3>
            <div>Yes with proper protocols: (1) written patient consent for photo capture + usage across social + ads + website, (2) consistent lighting + angle + framing before + after, (3) disclaimer 'Results vary. Consultation required.' overlaid on every image, (4) no unauthorized medical device brand names, (5) treatment specifics + timeline noted in caption, (6) never before-after of pediatric patients without parent consent. ITD's compliance advisor reviews every before-after asset.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do you shoot compliance-safe testimonials for dermatology?</h3>
            <div>ITD testimonial protocol: (1) signed video release from patient covering social + ads + website + edited versions, (2) patient chooses full-name or first-name-only or anonymized, (3) medical details discussed only with patient consent + doctor's review, (4) no unrealistic outcome claims in patient words (we prompt-guide during shoot), (5) disclaimer overlay 'Individual results vary. Consultation required.', (6) archive of consent for 3 years.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Do you produce content for both Reels + long-form YouTube?</h3>
            <div>Yes — one shoot day serves both. Reels get 15-60 second edits of the most social-friendly moments. Long-form YouTube gets 3-8 minute educational + testimonial deep-dives for high-AOV procedure research (patients spend 20-40 min on YouTube researching cosmetic surgery, IVF, hair transplant, cardiac procedures). Both channels compound organic reach + AI Overview visibility.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How does on-site shooting improve Instagram Reels performance for dermatology?</h3>
            <div>On-site shoots vs client-filmed content typically deliver: (1) 3-6x higher Reels engagement (professional lighting + framing + audio), (2) 2-4x higher completion rate (better hooks + pacing), (3) 30-50% higher DM conversion rate (trust + authority signals from production quality), (4) content library depth (4-8 Reels per shoot vs 1-2 client-filmed/week), (5) doctor + team confidence on-camera compounds over time.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do you coordinate shoots across a multi-location dermatology chain?</h3>
            <div>Multi-location shoot ops: (1) quarterly per-location shoot schedule at Premium tier, monthly at Enterprise, (2) location-specific creative brief (city context + procedures + doctor mix), (3) location-shared vs location-specific asset planning, (4) 2-day shoot cadence for adjacent Mumbai metro locations, (5) travel + logistics + accommodation for Pune / Nashik / Nagpur, (6) centralized asset library + per-location publishing rights.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What equipment does ITD use for dermatology shoots?</h3>
            <div>Camera: Sony A7 IV / Canon R6 II / Sony ZV-E10 (Reels). Audio: Rode Wireless Go II + shotgun for interviews. Lighting: Amaran 200D + softbox key + fill + rim + reflectors. Stabilization: DJI RS 3 gimbal + tripods. Lenses: 24-70 f/2.8, 70-200 f/2.8, 35mm f/1.4 prime. Grip: light stands + backdrops + diffusers. All owned + serviced + brought on-site by ITD team.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do you shoot a dermatology clinic ethically + safely for staff + patients?</h3>
            <div>ITD's ethical shoot protocol: (1) staff briefing on shoot day + participation is voluntary, (2) patient consent for any images/video with identifiable details, (3) medical equipment shot without patient-identifying context, (4) infection control + PPE observed during procedure filming, (5) HIPAA-adjacent Indian privacy standards on data storage + retention, (6) all assets archived on encrypted client-owned Google Drive.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Can we shoot with a mobile phone instead of hiring ITD&#x27;s team?</h3>
            <div>Possible but sub-optimal for Dermatology + Skin Clinics: (1) iPhone 15 Pro shoots decent Reels but lacks depth + lighting control, (2) doctor+ team direction takes 3-4 hours per Reel without director, (3) inconsistent quality damages brand trust in premium AOV specialties, (4) compliance oversights common without on-site review, (5) opportunity cost of doctor's time (Rs 3-15K/hour) exceeds shoot cost. Recommend: hybrid — ITD quarterly shoot + phone-shot content for daily velocity.</div>
          </div>
      </div>
